
public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
	    
		int arr[]={3,2,5,7,10,0};
		int n=arr.length;
		
		
		for(int i=0;i<n-1;i++)
		{
		    int minIndex=i;
		    for(int j=i+1;j<n;j++)
		    {
		        if(arr[j]<arr[minIndex])
		        {
		            minIndex=j;
		        }
		    }
		    int temp=arr[minIndex];
		    arr[minIndex]=arr[i];
		    arr[i]=temp;
		}
		
		
	}
}

//sort based on height order
⏱️ Time Complexity: O(n²)---------It always performs (n - 1) + (n - 2) + ... + 1 comparisons, regardless of input order.

💾 Space Complexity: O(1)--------- It sorts the array in-place using only a constant amount of extra memory.
